     The Wizard of Yendor will never show up on the Astral
Plane; once you get there, he takes the rest of the game
off.  (The only way he can get there is to be alive next
to you when you activate the portal to go there yourself.)
The harassment which begins when you first kill him--or
perform the invocation ritual to get access to the deepest
level, if you do that without killing him--will continue
when you're on the Astral Plane, but the choice of having
him appear is no longer one of the forms of harassment.

     I won't disagree with "Gehennom is boring" (or rather,
becomes boring quickly), but I do disagree that the Astral
Plane is too easy or even anti-climactic.  All three of
the Riders are quite dangerous, and they're deliberately
weakened so that they can be killed off much more easily
than you'd expect for critters of their nature.  The worst
part of astral is that so many monsters trigger multiple
long messages over and over.  That's where the ability to
kill things fast is a real boon.  (I had a smiley here but
I'm not sure it's warranted.  Monotonous message barrages
aren't funny....)


